        "POSSIBLE COMPLICATIONS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "POSSIBLE COMPLICATIONS",
          "canonical_heading": "POSSIBLE COMPLICATIONS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Lavage oral cavity for 10–15 minutes for Esophageal perforation, esophageal stricture, alkaline batteries; for disc batteries give gastrointestinal obstruction, heavy metal 10–20 mL of water every 15 minutes until toxicity. battery is out of esophagus.",
              "pdf_page": 248,
              "printed_page": 166,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
        "EXPECTED COURSE AND PROGNOSIS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "EXPECTED COURSE AND PROGNOSIS.",
          "canonical_heading": "EXPECTED COURSE AND PROGNOSIS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Donotinduce vomiting, as this may expose",
              "pdf_page": 248,
              "printed_page": 166,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Nonruptured dry cell battery—excellent; esophagus to further injury. most pets pass on own within 48 hours.",
              "pdf_page": 248,
              "printed_page": 166,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "NPO or slurry feeding for 24–48 hours if",
              "pdf_page": 248,
              "printed_page": 166,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Ruptured dry cell battery—guarded, oral ulcerations are present. pending location of corrosive exposure and",
              "pdf_page": 248,
              "printed_page": 166,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Ulceration may not be visible in the oral amount of time before removal; esophageal cavity until 48 hours post exposure. injury worsens prognosis.",
              "pdf_page": 248,
              "printed_page": 166,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Wear gloves when cleaning up battery",
              "pdf_page": 248,
              "printed_page": 166,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Disc/button/lithium ion battery—guarded, debris, as leaked acid could cause injury to rapid removal is needed; significant injury, hands. including esophageal or gastric perforation,",
              "pdf_page": 248,
              "printed_page": 166,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Small, intact dry cell batteries in stomach can occur within 15 minutes of ingestion. should pass within 48 hours; evaluate all stools and if battery has not passed the pylorus in 48 hours, surgical removal is recommended.",
              "pdf_page": 248,
              "printed_page": 166,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Punctured dry cell batteries and disc/button/lithium ion batteries should be",
              "pdf_page": 248,
              "printed_page": 166,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        }
      }
